index 0000000..bad2b85
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/HARNESS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+# Portable engine experiment
+
+Base: https://github.com/wszqkzqk/PvZ-Portable at
+`98b659380014c89c3553fbb2839f5e5a84d6df3d`.
+
+This is an isolated engine feasibility test, not an RSI training run and not a
+`pvz_rl` evaluation. It uses the user's installed Steam GOTY resources. No game
+assets are included in this checkout. The original Steam executable is not used
+or modified by the experiment.
+
+## Build and run on this workstation
+
+The sibling `../msys64/ucrt64/bin` contains the local MSYS2 GCC/CMake/Ninja
+toolchain and runtime DLLs. Package signatures are verified by pacman.
+
+```powershell
+.\tools\build-harness.ps1
+$env:PATH=(Resolve-Path '..\msys64\ucrt64\bin').Path+';'+$env:PATH
+python .\tools\harness_benchmark.py `
+  --exe .\build-harness\pvz-portable.exe `
+  --resources 'E:\Steam\steamapps\common\Plants Vs Zombies' `
+  --output ..\portable-benchmark-new --episodes 20
+```
+
+Use a new output directory for each run. All profiles and caches must be written
+under its private `save` directory. `engine.log`, per-episode JSON and a final
+`report.json` are retained there.
+
+## Interface and scope
+
+`PVZ_HARNESS=1` selects the experimental adapter. It requires a private
+`-savedir` argument. The application still initializes SDL/OpenGL with a hidden
+window, but advances `Board::Update` without drawing frames or wall-clock sleeps.
+It is not yet a graphics-free server build.
+
+The adapter performs the title screen's music initialization explicitly. In
+experiment mode Foley playback is disabled: the normal implementation's
+wall-clock audio completion changes how many shared RNG draws it consumes.
+This makes paired engine runs reproducible, but their seeded sequence must not
+be equated to the original game with audio enabled. Gameplay rules are still
+provided by the Portable engine. App/game update counters are advanced together.
+
+Commands are read only from the owning process's stdin; responses start with
+`PVZRPC ` followed by JSON. No network port or OS mouse events are used.
+
+- `reset LEVEL SEED`: recreate Adventure 1-1 through 1-10 and skip its intro.
+  Card-choice levels use a fixed public starter loadout. Loading a level is not
+  evidence that the model has beaten it.
+- `state`: observe without advancing time.
+- `render`: write the current game frame to the private save directory's
+  `observation.ppm` without advancing time; the gameplay RNG is preserved.
+- `step TICKS SLOT ROW COL`: advance 1–1000 ticks (100 ticks/game second).
+  SLOT=-1 means wait. A nonnegative slot uses ordinary game placement handlers.
+- `quit`: close this experiment process.
+
+Observations contain current sun, waves, cards, plants, zombies, legal actions,
+terminal status, and mower activation ticks. They do not expose future wave
+contents or RNG state. Sun is collected automatically; no planting strategy is
+implemented. Benchmark actions are exclusively WAIT, so planting effectiveness
+and Jev integration are not validated by its throughput result.
+
+## Acceptance checks
+
+The benchmark tests same-seed replay after an intervening different seed,
+time freezing between commands, invalid placement rejection without mutation,
+and 20 seeded episodes reaching an actual terminal state without truncation.
+An additional full-episode replay after losses includes deliberate wall-clock
+pauses in one repetition. Those two validation episodes are excluded from the
+timed batch. Replay equality compares the observations exposed by the adapter,
+not every internal engine field.
+
+Report both observed wall time and game-time/wall-time ratio. Games/hour is an
+extrapolation from the measured batch, not a long-duration stability result.
+Model inference, Coach/Engineer, parallel lanes and promotion are excluded.
+
+Before use as an RSI gate, validate real Jev placements, winning episodes,
+additional levels, fidelity against the installed game, stable observation/action
+contracts, and separate backend/version identities for candidate and incumbent.
+
+## Original narrow prototype result (2026-10-31, this Windows workstation)
+
+Final output: `../../portable-benchmark-20261031-final/report.json`.
+
+- 20 Adventure 1-4 WAIT-only episodes, seeds 50000–50019; all reached loss.
+- Batch wall time: **1.4740593 s**, including resets and observation I/O.
